moving_average.ino<pre><code>const int N = 16;
int buffer[N];          // last N readings
int pos = 0;            // where the next one goes
long sum = 0;

void setup() { Serial.begin(115200); }

void loop() {
  int raw = analogRead(36);
  sum -= buffer[pos];         // remove oldest
  buffer[pos] = raw;          // store newest
  sum += raw;
  pos = (pos + 1) % N;        // wrap around
  int filtered = sum / N;

  Serial.printf("raw:%d,filtered:%d\n", raw, filtered);
  delay(20);
}
</code></pre> <p>Download this example</p> <ul> <li> <p>A circular buffer: <code>pos</code> runs 0 … 15, 0 … 15 thanks to <code>% N</code>.</p> </li> <li> <p>Keep a running <code>sum</code>: subtract the oldest, add the newest. No inner loop needed.</p> </li> <li> <p>Open the Serial Plotter: the filtered line is smooth but reacts slower.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Trade-off</p> <p>Larger N = smoother but slower. Choose N for your signal.</p>

