</code></pre> <p>Download this example</p> <ul> <li> <p>Diagram circles become enum values.</p> </li> <li> <p><code>enterState()</code> stores both the state and its entry time.</p> </li> <li> <p>Every transition goes through this function.</p> </li> <li> <p>Serial reports each transition once.</p> </li> <li> <p>Startup leaves the simulated pump off.</p> </li> </ul>

plant-watering.ino (2/2)<pre><code>void loop() {
  unsigned long now = millis();
  switch (state) {
    case CHECK_SOIL: {
      int moisture = map(analogRead(SENSOR), 0, 4095, 0, 100);
      if (moisture &lt; 30) enterState(WATERING, now);
      break;
    }
    case WATERING:
      if (now - enteredAt &gt;= 10000UL)
        enterState(SOAKING, now);
      break;
    case SOAKING:
      if (now - enteredAt &gt;= 60000UL)
        enterState(CHECK_SOIL, now);
      break;
    default:
      enterState(CHECK_SOIL, now);
      break;
  }
  digitalWrite(PUMP_LED, state == WATERING ? HIGH : LOW);
}
</code></pre> <p>Download this example</p> <ul> <li> <p><code>CHECK_SOIL</code>: decide whether watering is needed.</p> </li> <li> <p><code>WATERING</code>: leave after 10 s.</p> </li> <li> <p><code>SOAKING</code>: leave after 60 s.</p> </li> <li> <p>Outputs follow the resulting state on every iteration.</p> </li> <li> <p>No waiting loop and no <code>delay()</code>.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Check the diagram</p> <p>Try 50 %, then 20 %. Restore 50 % while watering: does it still finish the 10 s phase and then wait 60 s?</p>

kitchen-timer.ino (1/3)<pre><code>// Course board: KEY1 starts/cancels/acknowledges a fixed 10-second timer.
enum TimerState { READY, RUNNING, DONE };
TimerState state = READY;
const int BUTTON = 34, BLUE_LED = 23, RED_LED = 21;
const unsigned long DURATION = 10000UL;
unsigned long enteredAt = 0;

bool pressEvent(unsigned long now) {
  static bool lastRaw = false, stable = false;
  static unsigned long changedAt = 0;
  bool raw = digitalRead(BUTTON) == HIGH;
  if (raw != lastRaw) {
    lastRaw = raw;
    changedAt = now;
  }
  if (now - changedAt &lt; 30UL || raw == stable) return false;
  stable = raw;
  return stable;  // true only on a debounced LOW-to-HIGH edge
}
</code></pre> <p>Download this example</p> <ul> <li> <p>KEY1 uses the course-board external pull-down: pressed is HIGH.</p> </li> <li> <p>Record when the raw reading changes.</p> </li> <li> <p>Accept the new value after it stays stable for 30 ms.</p> </li> <li> <p>Return true only when the accepted value changes to HIGH.</p> </li> <li> <p>The same event has a different action in each state.</p> </li> </ul>

