kitchen-timer.ino (3/3)<pre><code>void loop() {
  unsigned long now = millis();
  bool pressed = pressEvent(now);
  switch (state) {
    case READY:
      if (pressed) enterState(RUNNING, now);
      break;
    case RUNNING:
      if (pressed) enterState(READY, now);  // cancel has priority
      else if (now - enteredAt &gt;= DURATION) enterState(DONE, now);
      break;
    case DONE:
      if (pressed) enterState(READY, now);
      break;
    default:
      enterState(READY, now);
      break;
  }
  digitalWrite(BLUE_LED, state == RUNNING ? HIGH : LOW);
  bool flash = ((now - enteredAt) / 250UL) % 2 == 0;
  digitalWrite(RED_LED, state == DONE &amp;&amp; flash ? HIGH : LOW);
}
</code></pre> <p>Download this example</p> <ul> <li> <p>Read time and the button once per iteration.</p> </li> <li> <p>Compare every transition with the diagram.</p> </li> <li> <p>Use elapsed time for the alarm’s blink phase too.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Test it</p> <p>Start, hold the button, cancel, restart, wait for DONE, then acknowledge. Predict each LED before running the sketch.</p>

